# Batch files must reach cmd.exe with CRLF endings. With a bare LF, a caret
# line-continuation escapes the first character of the next line instead of
# joining it: "…' dailybot_data_'…" became the command "aily" and looped
# forever. See the maintainer note at the top of dailybot/backup_data.bat.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# PowerShell reads LF fine; keep the default (no rule) so the CRLF warnings
# from core.autocrlf stay meaningful for the .ps1 scripts.
